{
  "id": "cognitive-narrowing",
  "term": "cognitive narrowing",
  "definition": "Cognitive narrowing is a reduced, less thorough way of processing information during problem solving, marked by limited attention and disorganized exploration. In this study, it described the pattern shown by lower-resilience students, who examined less information deeply and were more likely to respond with random trial and error or give up when anxious.",
